@* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   TodayWeekTasksHubExplainer — clarifies that Today, Week and Tasks Hub are not
   competing task lists but three views of the same underlying work (issue #294).
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
<div class="ob-explainer" role="note" aria-label="How Today, Week and Tasks Hub work together">
    <p class="ob-explainer__lead">
        <strong>Today</strong>, <strong>Week</strong> and <strong>Tasks Hub</strong> are not three separate
        to-do lists — they are three views onto the same tasks.
    </p>
    <ul class="ob-explainer__points">
        <li><strong>Today</strong> is where you execute: your current focus and what's due right now.</li>
        <li><strong>Week</strong> is where you plan ahead: commitments you deliberately pull into the coming days.</li>
        <li><strong>Tasks Hub</strong> is where you organize everything by project, priority, and status.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="ob-explainer__foot">
        A task created anywhere shows up everywhere it belongs — there is nothing to keep in sync by hand.
    </p>
</div>

